# A here-document combined with an ordinary redirect on the same command: `cat
# <<EOF >out` opens a heredoc AND redirects stdout. The HeredocRedirect and the
# Redirect both attach to the simple command; the heredoc body still drains after
# the line's newline.
<<<cmd
printf 'cat <<EOF >out\nx\nEOF\n' | "$TP" run std.shell --input - --dump-tree
<<<assert
exit 0
out-absent ERROR
out-absent MISSING
out-count 1 HeredocRedirect
out-count 1 redirect: Redirect
out-count 1 HeredocBody [
